---
import ArtworkMeta from "../../components/art/ArtworkMeta.astro"
---

<div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
  <ArtworkMeta fields={[
    { label: "Year", value: "2023" },
    { label: "Medium", value: "Net art · Website, computer, sound, single channel" },
    { label: "Duration", value: "Variable" },
    { label: "Exhibition", value: "The Wrong Biennale 2023 · Un_Unsubscribe pavilion" },
    { label: "Curators", value: "Khristina Ots & Roman Solodkov" },
    {
      label: "Link",
      value: '<a href="https://poetic-garden.netlify.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: inherit;">poetic-garden.netlify.app</a>',
      html: true,
    },
  ]} />

  <p class="mb-4">
    Write a poem, press the Alt key, and the garden takes the words — the text mutates while a
    dithered tree grows from what the poem gives up. Better played with sound on.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    Exhibited in The Wrong Biennale 2023 within <em>Un_Unsubscribe</em>, a pavilion curated by
    Khristina Ots and Roman Solodkov exploring affective intensities and regimes of digital
    aesthetics — from poor images to file mobility.
  </p>

  <p>
    Play it at
    <a href="https://poetic-garden.netlify.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">poetic-garden.netlify.app</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="art-media-grid">
    <figure class="art-media-full">
      <img
        src="/images/poetic-garden/poetic-garden-capture.jpg"
        alt="Poetic Garden — a poem typed into the browser, its mutated lines accumulating as a dithered tree grows beneath the text"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>
